## ─── Profiles ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
## Profiles live in the database, not in files: add one in the web editor
## (Today page, or Settings -> + Add profile): a name and its web sign-in
## password, typed twice. Garmin and a Renpho scale are optional and connected
## per profile in Settings.
##
## Upgrading from the old .env.<profile> files (GARMIN_EMAIL, GARMIN_PASSWORD,
## WEB_PASSWORD): they are not read any more; import them once with
##   npm run store -- import-env <directory of the files>
##
## Usage:
##   npm run mcp -- --profile Julie
## ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─── MCP server (claude.ai / Claude Desktop) ──────────────────────────────────
# See "MCP Server" in README.md. In Docker these go in the compose .env file.

# Required for HTTP mode, at least 32 characters:  openssl rand -hex 32
# MCP_AUTH_TOKEN=
# Profile used when a tool call doesn't name one (optional if you have only one)
# GARMIN_PROFILE=MED
# MCP_PORT=8787
# MCP_HOST=127.0.0.1

# Encrypts the logins saved in the web editor's Settings view (Garmin, Renpho) in the database:  openssl rand -hex 32
# Put the same value in every service that shares the database (the MCP server and the web editor; docker-compose.yml passes it to
# both). Keep it with the deployment, not in the database or its backups. Without it, saved passwords are stored as plain text,
# and both servers say so at start-up. The Garmin session tokens in the database are not encrypted either way.
# CREDENTIALS_KEY=

# Plan editor web UI (npm run web); a token is required when WEB_HOST is not loopback
# WEB_PORT=8788
# WEB_HOST=127.0.0.1
# WEB_AUTH_TOKEN=                 # admin login (any user name); each profile signs in with its own password, set in Settings
# Behind a Cloudflare Tunnel or reverse proxy every visitor reaches the editor from the proxy's address, so the limit on wrong
# passwords (10 a minute per address) would count everyone together and anyone could lock you out. Name the header that tells the
# visitor apart:  cloudflare (CF-Connecting-IP)  or  proxy (the last X-Forwarded-For entry). Only when the proxy alone can reach
# the editor's port: anyone who can connect directly could send the header. Unset: the connection's own address.
# TRUST_PROXY=cloudflare

# The Food view's AI box (describe or photograph a meal, Claude estimates it). Two ways to ask Claude; without either the box says it is not set up.
#   cli: Claude Code's `claude -p` on your Claude plan (Pro, Max), no API credit. Run `claude setup-token` in your own terminal where you
#        are signed in to Claude, and put the token here. The Docker image has Claude Code installed.
#   api: the Anthropic API, paid from API credit (console.anthropic.com; a Claude plan includes none, except Max and Team).
# FOOD_AI_BACKEND=cli               # cli or api; unset: api when there is an API key, else cli when there is a token
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# FOOD_AI_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5   # default; claude-haiku-5-5 is lighter on the plan's limits and on the bill
# FOOD_AI_DAILY_LIMIT=30            # estimates a profile may ask for in a day (default 30)

# Docker compose only
# PUID=1000
# PGID=1000
# MCP_BIND=127.0.0.1
# WEB_BIND=127.0.0.1
# (compose also reads WEB_AUTH_TOKEN and WEB_PORT from above; WEB_AUTH_TOKEN is required; FOOD_AI_BACKEND, CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, FOOD_AI_MODEL and FOOD_AI_DAILY_LIMIT are optional)
# TUNNEL_TOKEN=

# Directory overrides (set by the Docker image; defaults match the CLI layout)
# GARMIN_DATA_DIR=/data           # per-profile data root           (default: <project>/data)
# GARMIN_STORE_PATH=/data/garmin.db  # the SQLite database          (default: <GARMIN_DATA_DIR>/garmin.db)

# Your time zone, for "today". Needed for a profile without Garmin; with Garmin the fallback is the offset your newest activity shows.
# GARMIN_TZ=America/Toronto       # (default: TZ)
# WELLNESS_DAYS=60                # days of sleep/HRV/... the background sync keeps (default: 60)
